Christ, but I want us to really wrestle with this. What does this mean for me? What does this mean

00:44:50.570 --> 00:44:55.850
for us? How do I not just say I believe in these truths like we recited the Apostles' Creed earlier,

00:44:55.990 --> 00:45:02.110
but how do I actually live in this? Myself, with God, and even in relationship with my brothers and

00:45:02.110 --> 00:45:06.910
sisters in Christ. So can I give us some things here to reflect and pray about as we close out

00:45:06.910 --> 00:45:11.590
our time here this morning? First question I want to ask us to think through is, how do you deal

00:45:11.590 --> 00:45:13.010
with the problem of sin in your life?

00:45:14.170 --> 00:45:14.990
How do you respond to that?

00:45:15.010 --> 00:45:15.970
Because all of us have sin.

00:45:16.650 --> 00:45:17.330
1 John says,

00:45:17.430 --> 00:45:18.650
if anyone claims they don't have sin,

00:45:18.690 --> 00:45:20.010
he's a liar and the truth is not in him.

00:45:20.650 --> 00:45:21.690
All of us have sin.

00:45:21.890 --> 00:45:23.110
There's not a single one of us who doesn't.

00:45:23.750 --> 00:45:24.630
How do we deal with that?

00:45:25.410 --> 00:45:26.250
How do we deal with that?

00:45:26.890 --> 00:45:28.290
I think what the world does

00:45:28.290 --> 00:45:30.190
around us who doesn't know Christ

00:45:30.190 --> 00:45:32.010
is hide from sin.

00:45:32.730 --> 00:45:33.850
Pretend it doesn't exist.

00:45:34.530 --> 00:45:36.190
Try to justify that sin.

00:45:36.270 --> 00:45:36.850
Oh, well, here's,

00:45:36.910 --> 00:45:37.790
I have this justification

00:45:37.790 --> 00:45:39.230
for why what I did

00:45:39.230 --> 00:45:40.570
